Subject: [PATCH] test/ossfuzz.c: call sqlite3_initialize() in LLVMFuzzerInitialize

LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput() calls sqlite3_initialize() for every input; the
first call does the one-time setup (sqlite3RegisterBuiltinFunctions(),
page cache and malloc subsystem init, about 45k wasm instructions) and
every later call returns at once. So the first input of each process, or
every input on a fresh instance, pays for it. Run it once from
LLVMFuzzerInitialize() instead; the per-input call stays and is then
always the early-out, as it already is in a persistent fuzzer after its
first input. ossshell.c, which calls LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput() directly,
is unaffected.

Upstream context: SQLite does not take pull requests; the GitHub mirror
has no open issue or PR about the fuzzer (checked 2026-11-20).

diff --git a/test/ossfuzz.c b/test/ossfuzz.c
index 8e80b98ef6..70fa63bd9b 100644
--- a/test/ossfuzz.c
+++ b/test/ossfuzz.c
@@ -112,6 +112,18 @@ static int exec_handler(void *pClientData, int argc, char **argv, char **namev){
   return (p->execCnt--)<=0 || progress_handler(pClientData);
 }
 
+/*
+** Run sqlite3_initialize() once at startup, so that its one-time setup
+** (built-in function registration, page cache and memory allocator
+** initialization) is not part of the first input.
+*/
+int LLVMFuzzerInitialize(int *pArgc, char ***pArgv){
+  (void)pArgc;
+  (void)pArgv;
+  sqlite3_initialize();
+  return 0;
+}
+
 /*
 ** Main entry point.  The fuzzer invokes this function with each
 ** fuzzed input.
